  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Lamplit Room",
    "overview": "The site is the owner's bedroom at night, built as a three-quarter cutaway diorama in React Three Fiber and held at an angled, mostly fixed camera. Charcoal plaster, smoked oak, a wool rug and matte fabrics sit in soft low light from a ceiling fill, a warm desk lamp and nightstand lamp, moonlight through the window, and the cool spill of the monitor. Colour enters the room only through the objects the visitor can use: the blaugrana jersey, the yellow plush, the cool monitor. Everything else is muted so those objects read as the navigation.\n\nOver the room sits a quiet HTML layer: near-black, glass-free panels with bone text, one grotesk, and hairline dividers. Every object leads to a panel that is ordinary, readable, linkable HTML; the 3D never carries content the HTML does not also carry. The monitor's cool white is the HTML layer's single accent, so focus, links and the active state all feel lit by the same screen. Interest pages swap that accent for their object's own colour.\n\nThe system is dense but calm: a recruiter can skip the room entirely through the menu, and nothing moves unless the visitor asks it to.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "A real room as the navigation; four objects plus the seated figure, each with one destination.",
      "Low, warm-and-cool practical lighting; colour only from the objects.",
      "Flat near-black HTML panels with 1px hairlines, no shadows, no blur.",
      "One variable grotesk (Schibsted Grotesk) at weights 400 to 700, including 550 and 650.",
      "One accent per panel: monitor-cool by default, the object's colour on interest pages.",
      "Motion only on request (hover, click, back); a faint monitor shimmer is the only ambient movement."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Objects Carry the Colour Rule",
        "body": "Architecture, furniture and fabrics stay muted (saturation low, roughness high). Saturated colour belongs only to the interactive objects and the monitor's light. A new object earns colour by being navigable.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Accent Per Panel Rule",
        "body": "A panel has exactly one accent: monitor-cool by default, or its object's colour on an interest page via the accent swap. Never mix two accents in one panel.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Weight Not Face Rule",
        "body": "Hierarchy is weight and size inside one family. Do not introduce a second typeface, uppercase labels, or wide letterspacing.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Depth Lives in the Room Rule",
        "body": "The 3D scene owns light, shadow and perspective. HTML surfaces stay flat and opaque so text never sits on a moving picture.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Own Colour Lift Rule",
        "body": "On hover or keyboard focus, every surface of the object (minus the screen) glows faintly in its own colour: emissive becomes the material colour at 32%. Near-black materials whose lifted colour sums under 0.18 get a cool floor (0.06, 0.07, 0.10) so the monitor, tower and camera read as clearly as the bright objects. The monitor's spill light also rises from 3.2 to 6. The label appears and the cursor becomes a pointer. Nothing scales, moves or outlines.",
        "section": "components"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Still Room Rule",
        "body": "The only ambient motion is the monitor spill light breathing (±0.12 on a slow sine). No floating, bobbing, spinning or particles. Under reduced motion the shimmer stops, the camera cuts instead of easing, and CSS transitions collapse to 0.01ms.",
        "section": "components"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** make every new interactive object lead to one real, linkable HTML destination, and add it to the object list so it is reachable without the 3D.",
      "**Do** give new room furniture muted colour and high roughness (0.6 to 1); reserve saturated colour for objects the visitor can use.",
      "**Do** light hover in the object's own colour at 32% emissive, with the cool floor for near-black materials.",
      "**Do** keep each panel to one accent, swapping it for the object's colour on interest pages.",
      "**Do** build panel content as hairline-divided lists and label/body rows that collapse below 620px of container width.",
      "**Do** mark missing content with a dashed frame or \"Link coming soon\" in Ash, and say plainly what is coming.",
      "**Do** show a button only when its action works; the résumé download appears only once a PDF exists."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** add neon, bloom, coloured outlines or glowing edges to objects; the only glows are the room's real light sources (lamps, monitor, window, LEDs).",
      "**Don't** add ambient animation beyond the monitor shimmer: no floating, bobbing, auto-rotating or particles.",
      "**Don't** add shadows, backdrop blur or translucent glass to HTML panels.",
      "**Don't** put content only in the 3D scene; the room is a way in, not the place content lives.",
      "**Don't** render placeholders as working links or buttons, or fill a page with empty media frames.",
      "**Don't** invent apps, metrics, users or achievements to fill a list; use an empty state.",
      "**Don't** add a second typeface, uppercase labels, or letterspaced small caps."
    ]
  }
}
